WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.875
To sum up.

2
00:00:00.875 --> 00:00:04.046
You created the compliant
network policy in report-only,

3
00:00:04.046 --> 00:00:07.083
read what it would have blocked,
proved that it blocks a

4
00:00:07.083 --> 00:00:10.187
sign-in without the client,
and put it back in report-only.

5
00:00:10.187 --> 00:00:14.988
Then you turned on universal tenant
restrictions and tested all four cases.

6
00:00:14.988 --> 00:00:17.917
The evidence an I S S O
keeps from this module:

7
00:00:17.917 --> 00:00:22.310
the policy export and the named
location, the report-only results,

8
00:00:22.310 --> 00:00:27.273
the disable-and-retry record, the
break-glass rehearsal record, the tenant

9
00:00:27.273 --> 00:00:29.877
restrictions exports, the tagging GET,

10
00:00:29.877 --> 00:00:33.050
the four-case record, and
the block query result.

11
00:00:33.050 --> 00:00:37.523
Next is Module 4, private applications
and administrative paths,

12
00:00:37.523 --> 00:00:42.620
where each application gets its own path
instead of the V P N's address pool.
